# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# notify-api environment variables
#
# DATA RESIDENCY — MANDATORY constraints (spec 005, CLAUDE.md):
#   1. EU region: this service MUST be deployed to an EU region only.
#      Production target: Railway EU (europe-west4) — see railway.json.
#      No notification data may be stored outside the EU.
#   2. No body logging: request/response bodies (notification title/body may
#      name clients/estimates) must NEVER appear in application logs.
#      hono/logger is configured to emit method+path+status only (see
#      src/index.ts). Do NOT add any logger that includes body, query
#      parameters with content, or the Prisma 'query' log level.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local: point at the compose Postgres (host port 5435, 'notify' database).
# Production (Railway): use the Railway-provisioned Postgres URL (Railway EU).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5435/notify

# ─── CORS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of allowed origins (no wildcards).
# Must include the shell origin(s) for each environment (the SSE stream's
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin is pinned to the shell origin — plan.md).
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000

# ─── Auth (JWT resource-server verification) ─────────────────────────────────
# auth service JWKS endpoint — used by jwtMiddleware to verify RS256 tokens.
# Both values are required; the service will refuse to start if either is missing.
#
# IMPORTANT: use /auth/jwks (better-auth's built-in JWKS endpoint) NOT
# /.well-known/jwks.json — the latter serves the env-var key (kid:
# operai-auth-rs256-v1) which is a DIFFERENT key from the one better-auth's
# jwt plugin uses (stored in the jwks table, dynamic kid). The /auth/token
# endpoint signs with the DB keypair, so notify-api must verify against
# /auth/jwks.
AUTH_JWKS_URL=http://localhost:3001/auth/jwks
AUTH_ISSUER=http://localhost:3001

# ADR-0010: notify-api is the suite's first real second JWKS resource server —
# a token minted for estimai-api is structurally valid at notify-api and vice
# versa unless both verify a shared `aud` claim. This value MUST be byte-for-byte
# identical to the `AUTH_AUDIENCE` the `auth` service stamps on every JWT
# (auth/.env.example). A token with a missing or mismatched audience is
# rejected with 401 by jwt.middleware.ts.
AUTH_AUDIENCE=operai-suite

# ─── SSE stream (T7, ADR-0008) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bounds how long a single GET /notifications/stream connection may stay open
# before the server closes it, forcing the client to re-ticket (plan.md
# §API contracts). Seconds. Default: 1800 (~30 min).
MAX_STREAM_DURATION=1800

# ─── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8081
NODE_ENV=development

# ─── Email channel (T2, specs/006-user-invitations, ADR-0011) ────────────────
# EMAIL_ENABLED gates whether the `email` channel makes a real Resend call.
# Default false — test/local NEVER need a Resend key: with it unset/false the
# channel stubs the send and still records an EmailDelivery row (status
# "sent", a synthetic providerId), so the invite-email flow is fully testable
# without a Resend account. Set to "true" (exact string) only when
# RESEND_API_KEY/RESEND_FROM are also configured (production).
EMAIL_ENABLED=false

# 1Password-sourced Resend API key. Required (service refuses to start
# without it) only when EMAIL_ENABLED=true. Data residency (plan.md Risk R5 /
# ADR-0011 compliance notes): use Resend's EU sending region where available —
# this is the transactional MTA, not data-at-rest, but prefer EU to match the
# suite's EU-only posture (CLAUDE.md).
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Verified Resend sending address/domain (SPF/DKIM configured on
# operai.welld.io — plan.md Risk R5; see infra/README.md for the DNS records
# to add before the first real send, or every message risks landing in spam
# or being rejected outright). Required only when EMAIL_ENABLED=true.
RESEND_FROM=no-reply@operai.welld.io

# ─── System-to-system auth (T3, specs/006-user-invitations, ADR-0011) ────────
# Shared secret validated by internalTokenMiddleware against the
# X-Internal-Token header on POST /system/emails ONLY. MUST be a strong,
# 1Password-sourced random value (>=32 chars), byte-for-byte identical to the
# `auth` service's NOTIFY_INTERNAL_TOKEN (auth/.env.example). Never logged by
# either service. A leaked value lets an attacker send arbitrary email over
# wellD's Resend domain (ADR-0011 Risks) — rotate + redeploy both services if
# compromise is suspected.
#
# UNCONDITIONALLY REQUIRED — unlike EMAIL_ENABLED/RESEND_*, this has no "off"
# mode: src/lib/env.ts enforces `min(32)` with no default, so the service
# refuses to start at all without it, even in local/test. For local dev,
# generate one with `openssl rand -hex 32` and paste the SAME value into both
# this file and auth/.env — a mismatch doesn't fail startup (both services
# just validate a nonempty/long-enough string independently), it fails every
# call to POST /system/emails with 401 at request time instead.
#
# PRODUCTION EXPOSURE (Risk R2): this endpoint must be reachable ONLY over
# Railway's private networking from the `auth` service — never rely on the
# public *.operai.welld.io domain being the sole gate. The token is the
# enforced access control regardless of network path; see infra/README.md
# § Variable reference for how `auth`'s NOTIFY_INTERNAL_URL is pointed at the
# private hostname.
NOTIFY_INTERNAL_TOKEN=
